description:
GOAL
The smallest complete semantic oracle for the entire canonical protocol: seals, intents, statement outcomes, net effects, decisions, refs, forge aggregates, outcome index, retention roots, and authority heads — as a pure, deterministic, no-I/O safe-Rust state machine (crate fgit-reference).

WHY / BACKGROUND
Every optimized implementation (per-core lanes, combiners, storage formats, indexes) must be trace-refinable to ONE reference semantics (plan §40.1/§40.5). Without an executable oracle, "correct" degrades into "what the implementation happens to do." The model is deliberately slow and simple; its only jobs are to be OBVIOUSLY right, replayable, and diffable. It is also the object FG-041's mechanized proofs will target, so keep its transition functions small and total.

MODEL SURFACE (from plan §10, §15, normative contract)
- TransactionSeal put-if-absent with byte-identical-retry / IdempotencyKeyReuse outcomes;
- ordered statements -> typed intents -> read-your-own-writes evaluation -> target-disjoint net-effect normal form (delegating detailed folding semantics to FG-008's component, which this crate hosts the interface for);
- DecisionSequence (every terminal admitted decision incl. refusals) vs RepositorySequence (committed transitions only) as distinct monotone sequences;
- RepositoryDecisionBatch/RepositoryCommitRecord/RepositoryAuthorityHead transitions with exact predecessor binding;
- CAS win/loss/ambiguity; cancellation semantics (no canonical Cancelled terminal; pre-seal vanish vs post-seal retryable);
- refusal taxonomy as typed values.

STRUCTURE: closes when subtasks (core model; golden traces + replay; exhaustive small-state campaign) close.

ACCEPTANCE (epic)
- no I/O, ambient time, randomized hash order, or runtime dependency (std only);
- operations consume an explicit snapshot and produce typed intents/effects/refusals;
- replay from genesis or any head yields byte-stable roots;
- model state serializes into golden traces via fg002 codec;
- a documented API by which implementation crates differential-test against this oracle.

FUTURE-SELF NOTES
Resist adding performance anything here — the model's slowness is a feature. When FG-041 mechanization arrives, any cleverness in these transition functions becomes proof debt.

CONSTITUTIONAL CONSTRAINTS (AGENTS.md; non-negotiable)
- Pure Rust, edition 2024, dated-nightly pin from rust-toolchain.toml; every first-party crate carries #![forbid(unsafe_code)]; no C/C++ FFI, no C Git/libgit2/JGit/Dulwich/gix, no hidden subprocess fallback. Upstream Git binaries are pinned, sandboxed differential ORACLES only (never production).
- Asupersync is the sole async runtime (no Tokio/async-std/smol). Long-lived work owns children via regions; cancellation is request -> drain -> finalize; effects use typed obligations (Reserved -> Committed -> Acknowledged, or Reserved -> Aborted).
- Closed dependency universe: every crate (incl. transitive, enforced via Cargo.lock scan) must match an active allow row in registries/dependency_policy.tsv. No build scripts/proc macros without a constitutional exception. No network during builds.
- Final-abstraction slices only: no empty crates, no HashMap-pretending-to-be-storage, no fixture-only parser wired as production API. A subset is fine when its unsupported surface is a typed refusal.
- Claim lattice (invariant > proof > bounded model > statistical > SLO > benchmark): never describe this work as stronger than its evidence. Record disproven hypotheses in docs/NEGATIVE_EVIDENCE_LEDGER.md + registries/negative_evidence.tsv.
- Run ./scripts/verify.sh fast before and after; stage only intended files; keep generated artifacts out of source.
